  "how_to_use": [
   "For a thoracic lateral bend of θ (T1 relative to L1, max one side ≈15.6 deg), distribute it per level in proportion to the 'mean of right and left' values (lower T10-L1 ≈36%, middle-lower ≈25%, upper ≈23%, middle-upper ≈16%).",
   "Use right/left rows only when side asymmetry matters (no significant difference, p≥0.2).",
   "Values are supine and submaximal vs standing; scale up if the standing thoracic LB (e.g. Narimani 2018 T1-T12 ≈25 deg) is the target."
